  "response_text": "If we didn\u2019t call __set_PSP(stackptr), the CPU wouldn\u2019t know where the thread's stack is. When the thread starts, it would try to pop register values from an invalid or zero PSP, leading to a hard fault because it tries to access memory it shouldn't. Setting PSP ensures the thread has a valid stack to start from.\\n",
